        "timestamp": 1775212313,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. The fight for mineral data in DRC: Belgian museum, US mining firm at odds over archive maps Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 12:31 Just a few kilometers from Brussels, the cellars of the Royal Museum for Central Africa hold one of the world’s most valuable mining archives. Colonial-era maps and surveys had previously detailed minerals like cobalt, lithium, coltan, and tungsten, essential for the digital and energy transition. Now, a battle over digitization is unfolding, with these documents literally worth their weight in gold. KoBold Metals, backed by Bill Gates and Jeff Bezos, is looking to AI in order to locate new deposits faster. Trump fires Pam Bondi as US attorney general 03/04/2026 Storm batters Greece, killing one, flooding homes and disrupting travel 03/04/2026 Weak enforcement blamed for building collapse that killed four in Ghana 03/04/2026 Viktor Orbán courts voters in neighboring Romania as Hungary’s election tightens 03/04/2026 Pain at the pump: How Europe is tackling rising fuel prices 03/04/2026 NATO members boost defence spending to cut reliance on US 03/04/2026 US-Israeli strikes destroy Iranian highway bridge 03/04/2026 Middle East How we came to be: Fossils rewrite origins of life on earth 03/04/2026 Hegseth ousts US Army chief of staff 03/04/2026"
